plunder and extort tribute across Sicily, as far as Gela and Camarina.", "lon": -52.488, "lat": -24.28}, {"year": -282, "title": "City of Phintias", "text": "Phintias, tyrant of Akragas, moves the people of Gela to a new city named after himself.", "lon": -57.364, "lat": -21.5}, {"year": -280, "title": "Rhegium seized", "text": "A Campanian legion garrisoning Rhegium for Rome massacres the citizens and takes the city.", "lon": -41.014, "lat": -9.296}, {"year": -278, "title": "Syracuse blockaded", "text": "A Carthaginian army and fleet besiege Syracuse; the city invites Pyrrhus of Epirus.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -21.984}, {"year": -278, "title": "Pyrrhus lands", "text": "Pyrrhus crosses from Italy to Tauromenium and marches on Syracuse, which hails him as king.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -12.437}, {"year": -277, "title": "Eryx stormed", "text": "Pyrrhus is first over the walls of Eryx; Panormus and the Punic west fall to him.", "lon": -70.271, "lat": -10.142}, {"year": -276, "title": "Lilybaeum holds", "text": "Two months of assaults fail against Lilybaeum, supplied by Carthage from the sea.", "lon": -71.705, "lat": -13.042}, {"year": -276, "title": "Pyrrhus departs", "text": "Pyrrhus sails back to Italy; Carthage's fleet mauls his ships in the strait.", "lon": -41.301, "lat": -7.725}, {"year": -275, "title": "Hiero chosen", "text": "The Syracusan army elects Hiero, a young officer who served under Pyrrhus, as its general.", "lon": -44.552, "lat": -21.742}, {"year": -274, "title": "Mercenaries sacrificed", "text": "Near Centuripe, Hiero lets his mutinous mercenaries be cut down by the Mamertines, then raises a citizen army.", "lon": -49.715, "lat": -15.217}, {"year": -270, "title": "Rhegium retaken", "text": "Rome storms Rhegium and executes the surviving mutineers in the Forum.", "lon": -41.014, "lat": -9.296}, {"year": -269, "title": "Battle of the Longanus", "text": "Hiero crushes the Mamertine army on the Longanus river near Mylae.", "lon": -45.126, "lat": -8.812}, {"year": -269, "title": "Hiero becomes king", "text": "Back in Syracuse, Hiero is acclaimed king; he will reign for over fifty years.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -21.863}, {"year": -265, "title": "Punic garrison", "text": "To keep Messana from Hiero, a Carthaginian squadron from Lipari puts a garrison in the citadel.", "lon": -47.707, "lat": -4.945}, {"year": -264, "title": "Rome crosses", "text": "The Mamertines appeal to Rome; the consul Appius Claudius crosses the strait at night.", "lon": -41.493, "lat": -7.966}, {"year": -264, "title": "Siege of Messana", "text": "Hiero and the Carthaginians besiege Messana together; Appius drives off both armies.", "lon": -41.971, "lat": -8.329}, {"year": -263, "title": "Hiero switches sides", "text": "With Roman legions at his gates, Hiero makes peace, pays a hundred talents and becomes Rome's ally.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -21.863}, {"year": -263, "title": "Segesta defects", "text": "Segesta kills its Carthaginian garrison and declares for Rome, its 'Trojan kin'.", "lon": -67.976, "lat": -11.35}, {"year": -263, "title": "Catana's sundial", "text": "Catana surrenders; the consul Valerius carries its sundial to Rome, the first in the city.", "lon": -46.369, "lat": -16.667}, {"year": -262, "title": "Siege of Akragas", "text": "Rome besieges Akragas, the Carthaginian base; Hiero's grain feeds the Roman camps.", "lon": -60.71, "lat": -19.204}, {"year": -261, "title": "Akragas sacked", "text": "Akragas falls after seven months; about twenty-five thousand people are sold into slavery.", "lon": -60.806, "lat": -18.963}, {"year": -260, "title": "Battle of Mylae", "text": "With boarding bridges on new-built ships, Duilius wins Rome's first great naval victory.", "lon": -44.934, "lat": -7.966}, {"year": -258, "title": "Camarina enslaved", "text": "Camarina falls to Rome and its people are sold into slavery.", "lon": -52.488, "lat": -24.28}, {"year": -258, "title": "Enna betrayed", "text": "The hill fortress of Enna is betrayed to the Romans.", "lon": -54.113, "lat": -15.821}, {"year": -256, "title": "Battle of Ecnomus", "text": "Some three hundred and thirty Roman and three hundred and fifty Punic warships clash off Ecnomus.", "lon": -57.364, "lat": -22.104}, {"year": -255, "title": "Fleet wrecked", "text": "A storm off Camarina sinks most of the Roman fleet with tens of thousands aboard.", "lon": -52.966, "lat": -24.884}, {"year": -254, "title": "Panormus taken", "text": "Rome takes Panormus, Carthage's main city on the north coast.", "lon": -62.909, "lat": -9.175}, {"year": -250, "title": "Battle of Panormus", "text": "Metellus routs Hasdrubal's army and captures his war elephants.", "lon": -63.196, "lat": -9.416}, {"year": -250, "title": "Siege of Lilybaeum", "text": "Rome begins a nine-year siege of Lilybaeum, Carthage's great fortress.", "lon": -71.705, "lat": -13.042}, {"year": -249, "title": "Defeat at Drepana", "text": "Claudius Pulcher attacks Drepana and loses most of his fleet.", "lon": -71.036, "lat": -10.383}, {"year": -248, "title": "Alliance for ever", "text": "Rome renews its treaty with Hiero without a time limit.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -21.863}, {"year": -247, "title": "Hamilcar on Heirkte", "text": "Hamilcar Barca seizes Mount Heirkte above Panormus and raids Italy's coast.", "lon": -63.005, "lat": -8.571}, {"year": -244, "title": "Hamilcar at Eryx", "text": "Hamilcar moves to Eryx and holds out between two Roman forces.", "lon": -70.271, "lat": -10.142}, {"year": -241, "title": "Aegates Islands", "text": "Lutatius Catulus destroys Carthage's relief fleet; Carthage gives up Sicily.", "lon": -73.522, "lat": -10.987}, {"year": -240, "title": "The Syracusia", "text": "Hiero's giant ship, designed with Archimedes' help, is launched; he later sends it to Egypt as a gift.", "lon": -44.552, "lat": -21.984}, {"year": -238, "title": "Grain for Carthage", "text": "During Carthage's mercenary war, Hiero sends it aid so that Rome does not grow too strong.", "lon": -44.361, "lat": -21.742}, {"year": -230, "title": "Theatre of Syracuse", "text": "Hiero rebuilds the great theatre, carving his queen Philistis' name into its seats.", "lon": -44.648, "lat": -21.742}, {"year": -227, "title": "A Roman province", "text": "Rome sends a praetor every year to govern western Sicily, its first province.", "lon": -62.909, "lat": -9.296}, {"year": -225, "title": "Altar of Hiero", "text": "Hiero builds an altar about two hundred metres long for public sacrifices.", "lon": -44.552, "lat": -21.742}, {"year": -218, "title": "Hannibal's war", "text": "Carthaginian ships raid Lilybaeum; old Hiero sails to Messana to greet the consul.", "lon": -41.971, "lat": -8.329}, {"year": -216, "title": "Gold after Cannae", "text": "After Cannae, Hiero sends Rome grain, a thousand archers and slingers, and a golden Victory.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -21.863}, {"year": -215, "title": "Hiero dies", "text": "Hiero dies at about ninety; within months Syracuse turns to Carthage.", "lon": -44.456, "lat": -21.863}], "eras": [[-289, -279, "The Sons of Mars"], [-278, -276, "Pyrrhus in Sicily"], [-275, -265, "The Rise of Hiero"], [-264, -241, "The First Punic War"], [-240, -219, "Hiero's Golden Age"], [-218, -215, "Hannibal's War"]], "refLine": null, "metrics": [{"label": "Syracusan lands", "stages": [2]}, {"label": "Roman lands", "stages": [4]}], "chartNote": "Share of the area of today's Sicily and Calabria, by the power holding each present-day province; regions are today's boundaries, not ancient ones. Each province takes the power that held its main city or most of its land, a simplification: Hiero's kingdom, for example, spread over parts of three provinces. Ancient dates are often uncertain by a year or two.", "chartTitle": "Who held Sicily, by area", "shares": [[0.7628, 0.1843, 0.0528, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [0.6824, 0.1843, 0.0528, 0.0804, 0.0, 0.0], [0.6824, 0.1843, 0.0528, 0.0804, 0.0, 0.0], [0.6824, 0.1843, 0.0528, 0.0804, 0.0, 0.0], [0.6824, 0.1843, 0.0528, 0.0804, 0.0, 0.0], [0.6824, 0.1